    "otherOrganization": "OpenTelemetry project",
    "introduction": [
      "Observability is the practice of understanding a running system from the telemetry it emits: metrics that quantify behaviour over time, logs that record discrete events, and traces that follow one operation across the components that serve it. OpenTelemetry is the vendor-neutral standard for that telemetry, and its protocol, OTLP, carries all three signal kinds to any conforming backend.",
      "An OPC UA Server already holds the values, events and diagnostics an observability backend wants. What it does not hold is a declaration of which of them are telemetry, what each one means, and how it maps onto the OpenTelemetry data model, so every integration is written by hand for one Server.",
      "This document defines that declaration. A Server states, in its own address space, which Nodes carry telemetry and how they map to OpenTelemetry, so that a generic bridge can export them without prior knowledge of the domain model."
    ],
    "draftBanner": "PROVISIONAL WORKING DRAFT — not normative, not endorsed by the OPC Foundation. The document number, the Mantis project identifier and every NodeId in this document are placeholders; the OPC Foundation assigns the real values."
  },
